On Windows the program uses WinFsp. It does not carry WinFsp and WinFsp is
not linked into it: when WinFsp is missing, the program downloads WinFsp's
own installer (winfsp-2.2.26323.msi) from the WinFsp project's GitHub
release, checks its size, SHA-256 and signature, and runs it with the
person's approval. A person may instead install WinFsp from its own
download page (https://winfsp.dev/rel/).

    WinFsp - Windows File System Proxy, Copyright (C) Bill Zissimopoulos
    https://github.com/winfsp/winfsp

WinFsp is licensed under the GPLv3 with the WinFsp FLOSS exception
(https://github.com/winfsp/winfsp/blob/v2.2/License.txt). The complete
source code of that release (2.2.26323) is at
https://github.com/winfsp/winfsp/tree/v2.2.

The notices of the open-source components linked into the program are in
internal/notices/NOTICE.txt; the program shows them with
"olsyn-drive licences" and on its About screen.
